The working of this Battery Level Indicator is based on voltage comparison using the LM3914 IC. 
The LM3914 internally contains 10 comparators. Each comparator corresponds to one LED output. 
When the battery voltage is applied to the input signal pin, the IC compares it with internally generated reference voltages. 
Depending on the voltage level: 
                A specific comparator activates 
                The corresponding LED turns ON 
                Higher voltage lights more LEDs 
Thus the LEDs provide a visual indication of the battery charge level.
